         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Images from Louvre\n\nThese images are copyright for Louvre and allowed to be used according to the license determined by them.\n\nTo visualize all images, use the left and right arrows on the slide below.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 3</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgLouvre0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgLouvre0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Levallois Core. © Musée du Louvre/ Département des Antiquités égyptiennes (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>The Mutapa State (<htdate0> - <htdate1>) - In this text, we study the development of the empire from an external perspective. (<htcite1>)</li><li>Great Zimbabwe - civilization built by the Shona people, one of the Bantu-speaking groups, in Zimbabwe. (<htcite2>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 3</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgLouvre1\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgLouvre1', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Foundation spout with inscription.. © Musée du Louvre (<htcite3>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Shimashki (<htdate2> - <htdate3>) - This \"lost\" kingdom dominated Elam after the fall of Awan. (<htcite4>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">3 / 3</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgLouvre2\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgLouvre2', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Tablet containing twelve kings of Awan. © Musée du Louvre (<htcite5>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Elamites – Dynasty of Awan - One list mentions three kings who ruled for 356 years (Sumerian King List). Another list presents twelve kings who ruled for about 200 years (List of the Kings of Awan). Why does this discrepancy exist? (<htcite6>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
